        "spya-jjfbqh",
        "spya-ne78jx"
      ],
      "title": "Mind, Morality, and Society",
      "gist": "Fowler extends phrenology's utility to morality, law, marriage, and public life, arguing that faculties explain both virtue and vice."
    },
    "n0073": {
      "id": "n0073",
      "depth": 2,
      "parent": "n0072",
      "children": [
        "n0074"
      ],
      "range": [
        "spya-jjfbqh",
        "spya-jjfbqh"
      ],
      "title": "Faculties, Virtue and Vice",
      "gist": "Every mental faculty is good in legitimate exercise but becomes destructive when overindulged, as illustrated by the fall of financier Mr. Hudson."
    },
